      },
      "cml:operator": "Classify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the provision as a prohibition using artificial intelligence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) It is unlawful for a person to subject another person to a workplace\nenvironment that is hostile on the ground of sex.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The provision classifies the behavior as unlawful."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-1-sec-28m-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28M(2) Hostile workplace environments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-1-sec-28m-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person (the first person) subjects another person (the second\nperson) to a workplace environment that is hostile on the ground of\nsex if:\n\n(a) the first person engages in conduct in a workplace where the\nfirst person or the second person, or both, work; and\n\n(b) the second person is in the workplace at the same time as or\nafter the conduct occurs; and\n\n(c) a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances,\nwould have anticipated the possibility of the conduct\nresulting in the workplace environment being offensive,\nintimidating or humiliating to a person of the sex of the\nsecond person by reason of:\n\n(i) the sex of the person; or\n\n(ii) a characteristic that appertains generally to persons of\nthe sex of the person; or\n\n(iii) a characteristic that is generally imputed to persons of\nthe sex of the person.\nNote:\nSee also section 8A in relation to workplace environments that are\noffensive, intimidating or humiliating for 2 or more reasons.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person (the first person) subjects another person (the second\nperson) to a workplace environment that is hostile on the ground of\nsex if:\n\n(a) the first person engages in conduct in a workplace where the\nfirst person or the second person, or both, work; and\n\n(b) the second person is in the workplace at the same time as or\nafter the conduct occurs; and\n\n(c) a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances,\nwould have anticipated the possibility of the conduct\nresulting in the workplace environment being offensive,\nintimidating or humiliating to a person of the sex of the\nsecond person by reason of:\n\n(i) the sex of the person; or\n\n(ii) a characteristic that appertains generally to persons of\nthe sex of the person; or\n\n(iii) a characteristic that is generally imputed to persons of\nthe sex of the person.\nNote:\nSee also section 8A in relation to workplace environments that are\noffensive, intimidating or humiliating for 2 or more reasons.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-1-sec-28m"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
