    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35F Giving of compliance notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, as a result of an inquiry into a person’s compliance with the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, the Commission\nfinds that the person is not complying, the President may give the\nperson a written notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) set out the name of the person to whom the notice is given;\nand\n\n(b) set out brief details of the failure to comply; and\n\n(c) specify action that the person must take, or refrain from\ntaking, in order to address the failure; and\n\n(d) specify a reasonable period (starting at least 21 days after the\nday the notice is given) within which the person must take, or\nrefrain from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(e) if the President considers it appropriate—specify a\nreasonable period within which the person must provide the\nCommission with evidence that the person has taken, or\nrefrained from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(f) set out any other matters prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph.\n\n(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If, as a result of an inquiry into a person’s compliance with the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, the Commission\nfinds that the person is not complying, the President may give the\nperson a written notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) set out the name of the person to whom the notice is given;\nand\n\n(b) set out brief details of the failure to comply; and\n\n(c) specify action that the person must take, or refrain from\ntaking, in order to address the failure; and\n\n(d) specify a reasonable period (starting at least 21 days after the\nday the notice is given) within which the person must take, or\nrefrain from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(e) if the President considers it appropriate—specify a\nreasonable period within which the person must provide the\nCommission with evidence that the person has taken, or\nrefrained from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(f) set out any other matters prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph.\n\n(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0c4c6949a56c67c6a3be6df5c8853cc7b63efab422c9f2bf101aa995dfbe23b9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35F Giving of compliance notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If, as a result of an inquiry into a person’s compliance with the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, the Commission\nfinds that the person is not complying, the President may give the\nperson a written notice.\n\n(2) The notice must:\n\n(a) set out the name of the person to whom the notice is given;\nand\n\n(b) set out brief details of the failure to comply; and\n\n(c) specify action that the person must take, or refrain from\ntaking, in order to address the failure; and\n\n(d) specify a reasonable period (starting at least 21 days after the\nday the notice is given) within which the person must take, or\nrefrain from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(e) if the President considers it appropriate—specify a\nreasonable period within which the person must provide the\nCommission with evidence that the person has taken, or\nrefrained from taking, the specified action; and\n\n(f) set out any other matters prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph.\n\n(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
