    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35F(3) Giving of compliance notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty",
      "skos:definition": "(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd4fef09a222ab9f68c2e205e7b62550c66a35f5b6ad51fa02316fc754c2e6e8",
      "skos:note": "Notice must not be given unless undertaking is withdrawn, cancelled or expired."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35F(3) Giving of compliance notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(3) However, if the President has accepted an undertaking from a\nperson under Part 6 of the Regulatory Powers Act in relation to the\npositive duty in relation to sex discrimination, a notice must not be\ngiven to the person under subsection (1) unless the undertaking is\nwithdrawn, cancelled or expired.\n\nSchedule 2  Positive duty"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35f-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If undertaking exists, then notice must not be given.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(President has accepted undertaking)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(Notice must not be given)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35G Reconsideration of compliance notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "President must reconsider compliance notice if requested\n\n(1) A person to whom a compliance notice is given may request the\nPresident to reconsider the compliance notice.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) be made in writing; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the request; and\n\n(c) be given to the President within 21 days after the day the\ncompliance notice is given to the person.\n\n(3) If requested, the President must reconsider the compliance notice.\nPresident may reconsider compliance notice on own initiative\n\n(4) The President may reconsider a compliance notice given to a\nperson without receiving a request if satisfied there is sufficient\nreason to do so.\nReconsideration\n\n(5) The President must act expeditiously in reconsidering a compliance\nnotice.\n\n(6) After reconsidering a compliance notice, the President must:\n\n(a) affirm the compliance notice; or\n\n(b) vary the compliance notice; or\n\n(c) revoke the compliance notice.\n\n(7) The President must give written notice of a decision under\nsubsection (6) to the person to whom the compliance notice was\ngiven, setting out the reasons for the decision.\nDecisions by delegates\n\n(8) If the President’s functions under this section are performed by a\ndelegate of the President, the delegate who reconsiders a\ncompliance notice:\n\n(a) must not have been involved in giving the compliance notice;\nand\n\nPositive duty  Schedule 2\nCompliance  Part 2\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\n(b) must hold a position, or perform duties, of at least the same\nlevel as the person who gave the compliance notice.",
      "skos:definition": "President must reconsider compliance notice if requested\n\n(1) A person to whom a compliance notice is given may request the\nPresident to reconsider the compliance notice.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) be made in writing; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the request; and\n\n(c) be given to the President within 21 days after the day the\ncompliance notice is given to the person.\n\n(3) If requested, the President must reconsider the compliance notice.\nPresident may reconsider compliance notice on own initiative\n\n(4) The President may reconsider a compliance notice given to a\nperson without receiving a request if satisfied there is sufficient\nreason to do so.\nReconsideration\n\n(5) The President must act expeditiously in reconsidering a compliance\nnotice.\n\n(6) After reconsidering a compliance notice, the President must:\n\n(a) affirm the compliance notice; or\n\n(b) vary the compliance notice; or\n\n(c) revoke the compliance notice.\n\n(7) The President must give written notice of a decision under\nsubsection (6) to the person to whom the compliance notice was\ngiven, setting out the reasons for the decision.\nDecisions by delegates\n\n(8) If the President’s functions under this section are performed by a\ndelegate of the President, the delegate who reconsiders a\ncompliance notice:\n\n(a) must not have been involved in giving the compliance notice;\nand\n\nPositive duty  Schedule 2\nCompliance  Part 2\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\n(b) must hold a position, or perform duties, of at least the same\nlevel as the person who gave the compliance notice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-7"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35g-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de0a16b3137fcbb8fda546d2fe6861446663bbce46e1944fd29e9be8b01ef4e5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35G Reconsideration of compliance notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "President must reconsider compliance notice if requested\n\n(1) A person to whom a compliance notice is given may request the\nPresident to reconsider the compliance notice.\n\n(2) The request must:\n\n(a) be made in writing; and\n\n(b) set out the reasons for the request; and\n\n(c) be given to the President within 21 days after the day the\ncompliance notice is given to the person.\n\n(3) If requested, the President must reconsider the compliance notice.\nPresident may reconsider compliance notice on own initiative\n\n(4) The President may reconsider a compliance notice given to a\nperson without receiving a request if satisfied there is sufficient\nreason to do so.\nReconsideration\n\n(5) The President must act expeditiously in reconsidering a compliance\nnotice.\n\n(6) After reconsidering a compliance notice, the President must:\n\n(a) affirm the compliance notice; or\n\n(b) vary the compliance notice; or\n\n(c) revoke the compliance notice.\n\n(7) The President must give written notice of a decision under\nsubsection (6) to the person to whom the compliance notice was\ngiven, setting out the reasons for the decision.\nDecisions by delegates\n\n(8) If the President’s functions under this section are performed by a\ndelegate of the President, the delegate who reconsiders a\ncompliance notice:\n\n(a) must not have been involved in giving the compliance notice;\nand\n\nPositive duty  Schedule 2\nCompliance  Part 2\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\n(b) must hold a position, or perform duties, of at least the same\nlevel as the person who gave the compliance notice."
    },
