    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35H Review of compliance notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who has been given a compliance notice may apply to the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) for a review of the notice on either or both of the\nfollowing grounds:\n\n(a) the person has not failed to comply as set out in the notice;\n\n(b) the notice does not comply with subsection 35F(2) or (3).\n\n(1A) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) if the compliance notice has been reconsidered under\nsection 35G—21 days after the person was given a notice of\na decision under subsection 35G(6) relating to the\ncompliance notice; or\n\n(b) otherwise—21 days after the day the compliance notice was\ngiven to the person.\n\n(2) At any time after the application has been made, the court\nconcerned may stay the operation of the notice on the terms and\nconditions that the court considers appropriate.\n\n(3) The court concerned may confirm, vary or cancel the notice after\nreviewing it.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who has been given a compliance notice may apply to the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) for a review of the notice on either or both of the\nfollowing grounds:\n\n(a) the person has not failed to comply as set out in the notice;\n\n(b) the notice does not comply with subsection 35F(2) or (3).\n\n(1A) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) if the compliance notice has been reconsidered under\nsection 35G—21 days after the person was given a notice of\na decision under subsection 35G(6) relating to the\ncompliance notice; or\n\n(b) otherwise—21 days after the day the compliance notice was\ngiven to the person.\n\n(2) At any time after the application has been made, the court\nconcerned may stay the operation of the notice on the terms and\nconditions that the court considers appropriate.\n\n(3) The court concerned may confirm, vary or cancel the notice after\nreviewing it.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-2-sec-35h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2880f2ccdbb3716e83677c41214360725eb0c08df2e62b22bb3ddb889f6179a7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-2-sec-35h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35H Review of compliance notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who has been given a compliance notice may apply to the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) for a review of the notice on either or both of the\nfollowing grounds:\n\n(a) the person has not failed to comply as set out in the notice;\n\n(b) the notice does not comply with subsection 35F(2) or (3).\n\n(1A) The application must be made within:\n\n(a) if the compliance notice has been reconsidered under\nsection 35G—21 days after the person was given a notice of\na decision under subsection 35G(6) relating to the\ncompliance notice; or\n\n(b) otherwise—21 days after the day the compliance notice was\ngiven to the person.\n\n(2) At any time after the application has been made, the court\nconcerned may stay the operation of the notice on the terms and\nconditions that the court considers appropriate.\n\n(3) The court concerned may confirm, vary or cancel the notice after\nreviewing it."
    },
