    {
      "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-58a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58A Victimisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-7-sec-58a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(1) It is unlawful for a person to commit an act of victimisation against\nanother person.\nNote 1:\nSee also section 42 (offence of victimisation).\nNote 2:\nSee also the definition of unlawful discrimination in the Australian\nHuman Rights Commission Act 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person (the first person)\ncommits an act of victimisation against another person if the first\nperson subjects, or threatens to subject, the other person to any\ndetriment on the ground that the other person:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a complaint under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(b) has brought, or proposes to bring, proceedings under this Act\nor the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\nagainst any person; or\n\n(c) has given, or proposes to give, any information, or has\nproduced, or proposes to produce, any documents to a person\nexercising or performing any power or function under this\n\nVictimisation  Schedule 7\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\nAct or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986;\nor\n\n(d) has attended, or proposes to attend, a conference held under\nthis Act or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act\n1986; or\n\n(e) has appeared, or proposes to appear, as a witness in a\nproceeding under this Act or the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986; or\n\n(f) has reasonably asserted, or proposes to assert, any rights of\nthe person or the rights of any other person under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(g) has made an allegation that a person has done an act that is\nunlawful by reason of a provision of this Part;\nor on the ground that the first person believes that the other person\nhas done, or proposes to do, an act or thing referred to in any of\nparagraphs (a) to (g), inclusive.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) It is unlawful for a person to commit an act of victimisation against\nanother person.\nNote 1:\nSee also section 42 (offence of victimisation).\nNote 2:\nSee also the definition of unlawful discrimination in the Australian\nHuman Rights Commission Act 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person (the first person)\ncommits an act of victimisation against another person if the first\nperson subjects, or threatens to subject, the other person to any\ndetriment on the ground that the other person:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a complaint under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(b) has brought, or proposes to bring, proceedings under this Act\nor the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\nagainst any person; or\n\n(c) has given, or proposes to give, any information, or has\nproduced, or proposes to produce, any documents to a person\nexercising or performing any power or function under this\n\nVictimisation  Schedule 7\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\nAct or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986;\nor\n\n(d) has attended, or proposes to attend, a conference held under\nthis Act or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act\n1986; or\n\n(e) has appeared, or proposes to appear, as a witness in a\nproceeding under this Act or the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986; or\n\n(f) has reasonably asserted, or proposes to assert, any rights of\nthe person or the rights of any other person under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(g) has made an allegation that a person has done an act that is\nunlawful by reason of a provision of this Part;\nor on the ground that the first person believes that the other person\nhas done, or proposes to do, an act or thing referred to in any of\nparagraphs (a) to (g), inclusive.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-58a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-58a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0c2326d81fabfd398d89a149927867516bf9aa708bcc6a6f6a333e6336aa5636"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-7-sec-58a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58A Victimisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(1) It is unlawful for a person to commit an act of victimisation against\nanother person.\nNote 1:\nSee also section 42 (offence of victimisation).\nNote 2:\nSee also the definition of unlawful discrimination in the Australian\nHuman Rights Commission Act 1986.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person (the first person)\ncommits an act of victimisation against another person if the first\nperson subjects, or threatens to subject, the other person to any\ndetriment on the ground that the other person:\n\n(a) has made, or proposes to make, a complaint under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(b) has brought, or proposes to bring, proceedings under this Act\nor the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\nagainst any person; or\n\n(c) has given, or proposes to give, any information, or has\nproduced, or proposes to produce, any documents to a person\nexercising or performing any power or function under this\n\nVictimisation  Schedule 7\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 85, 2022\nAnti-Discrimination and Human Rights Legislation Amendment\n(Respect at Work) Act 2022\n\nAct or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986;\nor\n\n(d) has attended, or proposes to attend, a conference held under\nthis Act or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act\n1986; or\n\n(e) has appeared, or proposes to appear, as a witness in a\nproceeding under this Act or the Australian Human Rights\nCommission Act 1986; or\n\n(f) has reasonably asserted, or proposes to assert, any rights of\nthe person or the rights of any other person under this Act or\nthe Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986; or\n\n(g) has made an allegation that a person has done an act that is\nunlawful by reason of a provision of this Part;\nor on the ground that the first person believes that the other person\nhas done, or proposes to do, an act or thing referred to in any of\nparagraphs (a) to (g), inclusive."
    },
