          "@id": "concept:anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022-sch-7-sec-18-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3fd871b331958b949f1c9e113fc97ed71c37cf0014733992e8fc21fdce243893",
      "skos:note": "Continues previous definition of unlawful discrimination despite amendments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/anti-discrimination-and-human-rights-legislation-amendment-respect-at-work-act-2022#sch-7-sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Transitional—pre-commencement acts of victimisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nDespite the amendments of the definition of unlawful discrimination in\nsubsection 3(1) of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\nmade by this Schedule, paragraphs (ca), (d) and (e) of that definition\ncontinue to apply, in relation to conduct that was engaged in before the\ncommencement of this item, as if those amendments had not been\nmade.\n\nSchedule 7  Victimisation"
    },
